# statistics/CHANGELOG

## 20261015

0.11.0: + Median; + Statistics::Enumerable mixin and the statistics-enumerable opt-in

1. + lib/Statistics/Median.rb: Median.of, as Percentile.of(values, 50)
2. + lib/Statistics/Enumerable.rb: the mixin: mean, median, variance, standard_deviation, percentile, q25, q75, iqr, covariance, correlation, linear_regression, histogram, each delegating to its module-function with self as the values
3. + lib/statistics-enumerable.rb: the opt-in; requires the core and does Enumerable.include(Statistics::Enumerable)
4. ~ Histogram#initialize: Coerce before the empty? guard, so that any Enumerable, Range included, may be passed.
5. ~ Covariance.of: Coerce before the size guard, for the same reason.
6. ~ lib/statistics.rb: + require_relative for Enumerable and Median
7. + test/Statistics/Median_test.rb
8. + test/Statistics/Enumerable_test.rb: the mixin, via a throwaway Enumerable class, and not via the patch; + a case which fails should an of-shaped operation module not be exposed by the mixin
9. + test/statistics-enumerable_test.rb: the patch, in a subprocess, so that it cannot leak into the suite
10. ~ README.md: + Two surfaces section (and the note that the patch, though not the mixin, wants Ruby 3.0); + Median section; /require 'statistics.rb'/require 'statistics'/
11. CHANGELOG.md --> CHANGELOG
12. ~ statistics.rb.gemspec: + Median and the Enumerable mixin in the description
13. ~ lib/Statistics/VERSION.rb: /0.10.0/0.11.0/


## 20260923

0.10.0: + LinearRegression

1. + lib/Statistics/LinearRegression.rb: slope, intercept, predict, residuals, r_squared, standard_error, to_s
2. slope is Covariance.of(xs, ys) / Variance.of(xs); r_squared is 1 - RSS/TSS, which is 1.0 for constant values of y
3. .new raises for sets of values of unequal size, for fewer than two points, and for identical values of x
4. standard_error is nil for fewer than three points, there being no degrees of freedom left
5. ~ lib/statistics.rb: + require_relative for LinearRegression
6. + test/Statistics/LinearRegression_test.rb
7. ~ statistics.rb.gemspec: + LinearRegression in the description
8. ~ README.md: Document LinearRegression.
9. ~ lib/Statistics/VERSION.rb: /0.9.0/0.10.0/

0.9.0: + Covariance, Correlation

1. + lib/Statistics/Covariance.rb (raises for sets of values of unequal size)
2. + lib/Statistics/Correlation.rb (Pearson's r; raises when a set of values is constant)
3. ~ lib/statistics.rb: + require_relative for Covariance and Correlation
4. + test/Statistics/Covariance_test.rb
5. + test/Statistics/Correlation_test.rb
6. ~ statistics.rb.gemspec: + Covariance and Correlation in the description
7. ~ README.md: Document Covariance and Correlation.
8. ~ lib/Statistics/VERSION.rb: /0.8.0/0.9.0/

0.8.0: + Mean, Variance

1. + lib/Statistics/Mean.rb
2. + lib/Statistics/Variance.rb (population by default, sample: for Bessel's correction)
3. ~ StandardDeviation.of: now Math.sqrt(Variance.of(values, sample: sample)), so the sum of squares lives in one place
4. ~ lib/statistics.rb: + require_relative for Mean and Variance
5. + test/Statistics/Mean_test.rb
6. + test/Statistics/Variance_test.rb
7. ~ statistics.rb.gemspec: + Mean and Variance in the description
8. ~ README.md: Document Mean and Variance.
9. ~ lib/Statistics/VERSION.rb: /0.7.0/0.8.0/


